# /etc/cfm/cfm.dnat_cpanel_bypass
#
# Source-IP bypass list for the cPanel PANEL DNAT chain installed by
# `cfm dnat cpanel on` (TCP 2082/2083/2086/2087/2095/2096/2222 ->
# 12082-12222). Packets arriving from any IP / CIDR listed here SKIP the
# DNAT redirect and reach cpsrvd / DirectAdmin directly, bypassing CFM's
# panel-side challenge + WAF + tunnel logic.
#
# Primary use case: cPanel-to-cPanel WHM Transfer Tool source hosts. The
# transport that whm_xfer_download-ssl uses for live rsync streams is a
# non-standard HTTP variant that breaks when wrapped by ANY HTTP-aware
# proxy. Adding the source server's IP here makes its inbound 2087 (etc.)
# connections land on cpsrvd directly, exactly as they would with
# `cfm dnat cpanel off`, while leaving panel filtering on for everyone
# else.
#
# Format (same as cfm.allow / cfm.deny):
#   - one IP or CIDR per line
#   - blank lines and `#`-prefixed lines ignored
#   - trailing `# comment` on data lines also ignored
#   - both IPv4 and IPv6 are supported
#
# Manage with the CLI rather than editing this file by hand:
#   cfm dnat cpanel bypass list
#   cfm dnat cpanel bypass add    84.54.49.205
#   cfm dnat cpanel bypass add    2001:db8::/64
#   cfm dnat cpanel bypass remove 84.54.49.205
#
# Changes take effect immediately if cpanel DNAT is currently on;
# otherwise they apply on the next `cfm dnat cpanel on`.

# Examples (uncomment to use):
#84.54.49.205         # peer-cpanel-01 (transfer source)
#192.0.2.0/24         # cluster management subnet
